usage: launch_right_camera_playback.py [-h]
                                       [--hardware | --test | --hardwaretest]
                                       [--recording RECORDING]
                                       [--camera CAMERA | --select-camera]
                                       [--list-cameras] [--recording-only]
                                       [--auto-run] [--model MODEL]
                                       [--imgsz IMGSZ] [--conf CONF]
                                       [--device DEVICE]
                                       [--preprocessing {local,reference,none}]
                                       [--lighting-profile LIGHTING_PROFILE]
                                       [--no-normalization] [--width WIDTH]
                                       [--height HEIGHT]
                                       [--allow-low-light-fps]
                                       [--process-every PROCESS_EVERY]
                                       [--output OUTPUT]
                                       [--audio-source AUDIO_SOURCE]
                                       [--audio-device AUDIO_DEVICE]
                                       [--esp-port ESP_PORT]
                                       [--mit-fall-kd MIT_FALL_KD]
                                       [--mit-inertia MIT_INERTIA]
                                       [--mit-brake-accel MIT_BRAKE_ACCEL]
                                       [--mit-latency-ms MIT_LATENCY_MS]

Right recorded-path camera alignment

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --hardware            one RUN button: center + close gripper, recording,
                        hybrid hit search, then 100 BPM swing
                        (camera/TONOR/ESP32)
  --test                pure simulation with no CAN, camera, microphone, or
                        ESP32; animate playback and fixed 10-degree strikes in
                        RViz
  --hardwaretest        run center/open/load, recorded playback, and single-
                        frame pink-zone alignment on the physical right arm;
                        then run one editable damped J7 freefall, predictive
                        catch and smooth MIT return per press (no ESP32)
  --recording RECORDING
                        right-arm recording (default: recordings/record1.json)
  --camera CAMERA       orbbec (default), camera index N, /dev/videoN, or a
                        stable /dev/v4l/by-id/ or by-path/ link
  --select-camera       choose a connected camera interactively before any
                        controllers launch
  --list-cameras        list connected camera names, indices and stable paths,
                        then exit without launching hardware
  --recording-only      physical no-strike test: recording, verified center,
                        then relax; never align or strike
  --auto-run            requires --recording-only: Run automatically, close
                        gripper after 5 s loading pause, exit after safe relax
  --model MODEL
  --imgsz IMGSZ
  --conf CONF
  --device DEVICE
  --preprocessing {local,reference,none}
  --lighting-profile LIGHTING_PROFILE
  --no-normalization
  --width WIDTH         RGB width (Orbbec full-FOV default: 1280; omitted
                        partner dimension inferred as 16:9)
  --height HEIGHT       RGB height (Orbbec full-FOV default: 720; cropped
                        modes are rejected)
  --allow-low-light-fps
  --process-every PROCESS_EVERY
  --output OUTPUT
  --audio-source AUDIO_SOURCE
                        stable PipeWire/PulseAudio TONOR TD510 capture-source
                        name
  --audio-device AUDIO_DEVICE
                        sounddevice input used by ST7 after selecting the
                        TONOR source
  --esp-port ESP_PORT   ESP32 motor_beat serial port (default: connected
                        CP2102 by-id path)
  --mit-fall-kd MIT_FALL_KD
                        hardwaretest only: gravity-descent damping (default
                        0.04)
  --mit-inertia MIT_INERTIA
                        hardwaretest only: loaded J7 inertia, kg m^2 (default
                        0.02)
  --mit-brake-accel MIT_BRAKE_ACCEL
                        hardwaretest only: calibrated catch acceleration,
                        rad/s^2 (default 40)
  --mit-latency-ms MIT_LATENCY_MS
                        hardwaretest only: command/actuation delay estimate,
                        ms (default 4)
